---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Files01DocumentImages from "../../components/Files01DocumentImages.astro";
import EvidencePanel from "../../components/EvidencePanel.astro";
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const volumes=[["C:","Windows and DFS namespace","63.15 GiB","34.39 GiB"],["D:","Company documents (NovaData)","59.98 GiB","59.49 GiB"],["B:","Windows backup target (NovaBackup)","99.98 GiB","97.98 GiB"]];
---
<BaseLayout title="Windows volumes and NovaData" description="Where Nova Corp stores Windows, company documents and file backups." breadcrumbs={[{label:"NOVA-FILES01",href:"systems/nova-files01/"},{label:"Windows volumes"}]}>
<section class="page-head"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">File server storage</div><h1>Windows volumes and NovaData</h1><p class="lead">The server separates Windows, company documents and backup storage into different volumes.</p></div></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="container prose"><h2>What is D:\NovaData?</h2><p>It is the folder on the dedicated D: data volume where Nova Corp keeps its five departmental folders.</p><h2>Why does it exist?</h2><h3 class="file-problem">Problem</h3><p>If company documents and Windows share one drive, growing department folders can consume the space Windows needs to operate. Keeping the backup on that same drive would also make recovery harder.</p><h3 class="file-solution">Solution</h3><p>IT created separate volumes: C: for Windows, D: for company documents and B: for the backup destination. Employees work in the same department folders while IT manages storage separately. This makes storage easier to manage, but the volumes are still inside the same nested lab failure domain.</p><h2>Storage specifications</h2><p>Historical recorded capacity and free space, not live readings.</p><div class="card-list">{volumes.map(([drive,purpose,capacity,free])=><div class="paper panel"><h3>{drive}</h3><p>{purpose}</p><p>Capacity: {capacity} · Free: {free}</p></div>)}</div><Files01DocumentImages ids={["fileserver-novadata-baseline","fileserver-backup-volume","fileserver-proxmox-hardware"]}/><EvidencePanel subject="Complete Windows volume view" requested="A single reviewed Disk Management or Get-Volume screenshot showing C:, D: and B: together is still needed; the original screenshots above establish separate parts of that configuration."/><h2>How to check it</h2><p>From the server, list volumes and inspect the departmental folders. These are suggested read-only checks, not a new recorded test.</p><pre><code>{'Get-Volume\nGet-ChildItem D:\\NovaData'}</code></pre><p><a href={base+"files/"}>Browse the five departmental folders →</a> · <a href={base+"files/backup/"}>Backup policy and tests →</a></p><p><a href={base+"reference/explore/files/VOLUMES/"}>Open the complete recorded storage inventory →</a></p><h2>Related incidents</h2><p><a href={base+"incidents/backup-target-unavailable/"}>Backup disk taken offline →</a></p><h2>Engineering journals</h2><p><a href={base+"pdf-journals/CR-012_Windows_Server_Backup_and_Recovery_Journal.pdf"}>CR-012 original PDF →</a></p><p><a href={base+"systems/nova-files01/"}>Back to NOVA-FILES01 →</a></p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.file-problem{color:#edb4a2;margin:24px 0 8px;font-size:1.05rem}.file-solution{color:#c6dcb4;margin:24px 0 8px;font-size:1.05rem}.prose,.content-section{min-width:0}.prose pre{max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto;box-sizing:border-box}.content-section details{margin:16px 0}.content-section summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:650}</style>
